[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     62[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 1. **Errors go to stdout, not stderr.** The C uses `printf` for both error
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     63[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    messages, so stderr is always empty even on the failure paths. A translation
