[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     69[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    rejects every one of them and would take the error branch instead.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     70[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 3. **`end == argv[1]` is the only error condition.** The check is "was anything
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     71[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    converted", not "was the whole string consumed". Trailing garbage is fine;
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     72[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `"  -  5"` (space between sign and digits) is not.
